.\" Man page for coyote_sqc — Coyote Session Quality Control application
.\" Generated 2026-06-21
.TH COYOTE_SQC 1 "2026-06-21" "coyote_sqc 0.1.0" "Coyote Manual"
.SH NAME
coyote_sqc \- Statistical Quality Control companion for the Coyote coding agent
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B coyote_sqc
[\fIworkspace.sqcw\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B coyote_sqc
is a standalone GTK3 application that reads Coyote session data,
computes Statistical Process Control (SPC) chart statistics, and
presents an interactive graphical analysis environment for process
monitoring, investigation, and annotation.
.PP
The application ingests Coyote session JSONL files from one or more
source directories, aggregates session-level and turn-level metrics,
and displays them as interactive control charts.  It does not write
to or modify Coyote session files; all application state (workspace
definition, chart setup intervals, comments) is stored in a separate
workspace file.
.PP
The application supports 91 pre-instantiated control charts across
six groups: Quantile Profiles, Token Consumption, Rates, Session
Totals, Token Costs, and Tool Call Behavior.  Chart types include
Xbar/s, Individuals (I), Moving Range (MR), Exponentially Weighted
Moving Average (EWMA), p-charts, and Quantile Control Charts.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fIworkspace.sqcw\fR
Optional path to a workspace file to open at startup.  If omitted,
the application starts with an empty workspace; the user can create
a new workspace or open an existing one via the File menu.
.SH "WORKSPACE FILE FORMAT"
Workspace files use the
.B .sqcw
extension and are stored as JSON.  A workspace contains:
.IP \(bu 2
One or more source directories to scan for Coyote session files.
.IP \(bu
An optional model filter (list of model identifier strings).
.IP \(bu
A setup interval \(em the set of sessions used to estimate control
limits for all charts.
.IP \(bu
Per-session comments for annotation and investigation tracking.
.IP \(bu
Per-chart settings (Box-Cox transformation, estimation method,
EWMA parameters, plot method).
.PP
The file format is versioned; the application refuses to open
workspace files with a version higher than it supports.
.SH "CHART GROUPS"
The 91 charts are organised into six groups in the left panel:
.TP
.B Quantile Profiles
Five Quantile Control Charts showing the empirical distribution of
per-turn observations (minimum, Q1, median, Q3, maximum) with
bootstrap control limits.
.TP
.B Token Consumption
Six Xbar/s chart pairs for per-turn token consumption: Turn Tokens,
Tool Call Tokens, and Thinking Tokens.
.TP
.B Rates
Eleven p-charts and I/MR/EWMA charts for event rates and token
ratios: tool-call failure rate, fraction of tool-call turns,
fraction of thinking turns, and various token-ratio charts.
.TP
.B Session Totals
Twenty-four I/MR/EWMA chart triplets for session-level totals:
Input, Output, Cache Read, Cache Write, Thinking, Tool-Call,
Tool-Call Result, and Uncached Input tokens, plus Turn Count.
.TP
.B Token Costs
Thirty I/MR/EWMA and Xbar/s charts for session-level and per-turn
token costs across six cost categories: Total, Input, Output,
Cache Read, Cache Write, and Uncached Input.
.TP
.B Tool Call Behavior
Fifteen charts for consecutive tool-call similarity analysis:
Jensen-Shannon divergence (JSD) and compression-based mutual
information (MI) diversity metrics, each with Xbar/s, I/MR/EWMA,
and Quantile CC variants.
.SH "STATISTICAL METHODS"
.IP \(bu 2
The only out-of-control rule is the 3-sigma rule: a point is
out-of-control if its statistic falls strictly outside the control
limits.
.IP \(bu
Control limits are variable \(em computed individually for each
point using that session's actual subgroup size.
.IP \(bu
All limit parameters are estimated exclusively from the sessions
in the user-designated setup interval.
.IP \(bu
Box-Cox transformation is available for I/MR/EWMA and Xbar/s
charts to correct skewness in token-count and cost data.
.IP \(bu
Robust (median/Q\(ssn\(es) estimation is available as an alternative
to classical estimators for control limit computation.
.IP \(bu
Quantile Control Charts use a two-stage bootstrap procedure
with Bonferroni multiplicity correction.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/coyote_sqc/config.json
Per-user application configuration (recent workspaces).
.TP
.I ~/.config/coyote_sqc/pricing.json
Per-model token pricing data in USD per token.  When absent,
pricing is resolved from the OpenRouter public model API.
.TP
.I ~/.config/coyote_sqc/openrouter_models_cache.json
Cached OpenRouter model catalogue (refreshed at most once per
application start; expires after 24 hours).
.TP
.I *.sqcw
Workspace files in JSON format, stored at a user-chosen location.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Start with a new empty workspace:
.EX
coyote_sqc
.EE
.TP
Open an existing workspace:
.EX
coyote_sqc ~/analysis/coyote-june.sqcw
.EE
